WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.362
The federal requirement, from
the guide's requirements table.

2
00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:09.225
Gate three supports four controls from
NIST special publication eight hundred

3
00:00:09.225 --> 00:00:14.387
fifty-three, revision five: S I three,
malicious code protection; S C seven,

4
00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:18.062
boundary protection, here
the host firewall; C M six,

5
00:00:18.062 --> 00:00:23.312
configuration settings; and S I seven,
integrity, here tamper protection.

6
00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:28.400
The evidence is the policy exports, the
device checks and the audit results.

7
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.975
Gate four supports C M seven, least
functionality, with C M six and S I three.

8
00:00:34.975 --> 00:00:37.567
The evidence is the rule-by-ring matrix,

9
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:41.537
with the date each rule entered
block, and the per-rule tests.

10
00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:45.644
Each row lines up with fed-ramp
twenty X key security indicators,

11
00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:50.913
which bind cloud service providers; the
agency lines its own evidence up with them.

12
00:00:50.913 --> 00:00:53.003
The gates support these controls,

13
00:00:53.003 --> 00:00:56.280
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.
